(D1b — Discrepancy 1, in the exact shape the generator already emits.
 `src/gen_misc.vox:383` emits a flag-reader function, and
 `src/gen_core.vox:963` rotates six prelude blocks so that the reader can
 be emitted BEFORE the flag schema it reads — deliberately, and the
 comment at `src/gen_misc.vox:369-375` records that this was hand-verified
 as legal Vox. It is legal. It is also one line away from printing a
 pointer.
 The reader as emitted survives only because it copies the text flag into
 a DECLARED text local first (`a text called fl1local is fl1label.`) and
 prints the local. This probe is that function with the copy removed —
 `Print fl1label.` straight from the forward-referenced global — and it
 prints a stack address. Run with no arguments so the flag takes its
 declared default `"d1"`; the top-level read prints `d1` and the
 in-function read prints the pointer.
 Same defect as D1.vox, reached through the generator's own prelude rather
 than a hand-written example. The address varies per run, so this probe
 is compared on its EXIT CODE: it exits 3 unconditionally.
